    {
      "name": "lighthouse-log",
      "note": "about 700 tokens: many 64-token Gated DeltaNet chunks before the question; the answer needs facts from the middle (March 9) and the end, and March 5 is a distractor",
      "kind": "chat",
      "messages": [
        {
          "role": "user",
          "content": "Keeper's log, North Skerry light, March 2031.\n\nMarch 1. Wind west-southwest, force 4. Air 6.5 °C at noon. Lamp lit at 18:12. Two fishing boats passed northbound before dusk. Replaced the cracked pane in the gallery door.\nMarch 2. Wind west, force 5, gusting 6 overnight. Air 5.8 °C. Lamp lit at 18:14. One cargo ship, the Morven, passed southbound at 15:40. Spent the afternoon greasing the rotation gear.\nMarch 3. Calm until noon, then wind north, force 3. Air 4.1 °C. Lamp lit at 18:15. No traffic. Counted forty-one gannets on the east ledge.\nMarch 4. Wind north-northeast, force 6. Air 2.9 °C. Sleet from 10:00 to 13:00. Lamp lit at 18:17. Three trawlers sheltered in the lee of the island until the wind eased.\nMarch 5. Wind northeast, force 7. Air 1.4 °C, the coldest reading so far this month. Lamp lit at 18:19. Four ships passed: two tankers, a ferry and a yacht under bare poles. The supply boat cancelled.\nMarch 6. Wind northeast, force 5. Air 2.2 °C. Lamp lit at 18:20. One tanker passed northbound. Cleared ice from the rain gauge twice.\nMarch 7. Wind east, force 3. Air 3.6 °C. Lamp lit at 18:22. Two coasters passed, both bound for the mainland. Painted the lower stair rail.\nMarch 8. Wind east-southeast, force 2. Air 3.0 °C. Fog from dawn until 11:30; the foghorn sounded for four hours. Lamp lit at 18:24. No traffic seen through the fog.\nMarch 9. Wind north, force 4, clear sky. Air −0.6 °C at 07:00 and only 0.8 °C at noon. Lamp lit at 18:25. Two ships passed: a research vessel and a cable layer. Frost on the gallery rail all day.\nMarch 10. Wind northwest, force 5. Air 2.7 °C. Lamp lit at 18:27. The supply boat arrived at 11:15 with diesel, flour and the post. Five fishing boats passed westbound.\nMarch 11. Wind west, force 4. Air 4.9 °C. Lamp lit at 18:29. One ferry passed. Tested the reserve lamp for thirty minutes; it ran without fault.\nMarch 12. Wind southwest, force 3. Air 7.2 °C. Lamp lit at 18:30. Three yachts passed southbound in the afternoon. Wrote the monthly fuel return: 212 litres of diesel used since March 1.\n\nUsing only the log above: on which date was the lowest air temperature recorded, what was the reading, and how many ships passed that day? Then state how much diesel was used since March 1."
        }
      ],
